how's it going everybody it's warren  welcome back to my channel the cosmic  wonder where we talk all things marvel  and  everything relating to the marvel  cinematic universe and  right now one of the biggest questions  out there that has not been answered yet  is will black widow and other future  marvel movies go  straight to disney plus as premier  access or are we finally going to be  getting a theatrical release for them  now we really don't have to worry about  other movies such as the eternals or  doctor strange in the multiverse of  madness or spider-man 3.  it's mainly just black widow that pretty  much a lot of the fan base at this point  in time right now are saying just  release it on disney plus so we can at  least see it  yes everybody believes that it deserves  a theatrical release but as of right now  we don't know if that will ever happen  over the weekend we got some news from  disney's ceo  and executive vice president that lead  us to believe that they may be  considering releasing black widow on  disney plus  and an announcement for it could be  coming very soon  so i'll break down what they said but  first if you're new be sure to subscribe  so you can stay up to date on all of the  latest mcu news and so you can enter  this week's giveaway for a chance to win  a tony stark funko pop i'm picking a  winner on friday  and thank you to skillshare for  sponsoring this video more on them later  on  so this past thursday disney's new ceo  bob chapack  hinted to wall street analysts during an  interview that disney is set to get more  aggressive in offering some  new theatrical titles via disney plus  paid download as it did in september  with mulan and as it's about to do with  disney's soul with many of the us  theaters shut down because of the  coronavirus disney made mulan available  on disney plus for  29.99 launching on their video on demand  service which they called premier access  and  on thursday bob chapek said that there  was enough traction with the premier  access release of mulan to encourage  them to do  more in this vein and then he said  something that was very very interesting  now there was a lot of controversy  around mulan about where they filmed the  movie  the controversy happened after the  release of mulan on disney plus and bob  chapek acknowledged that the controversy  did in fact hurt the film  and when he commented on it he said we  saw enough  very positive results before that  controversy started  we've got something there in terms of  the premier access strategy and then he  said that he has more details to come  on december 10th when disney holds an  investor day presentation  on its streaming strategy now a lot of  people are thinking that this could be  the announcement of black widow coming  to disney plus's premier  access after all very recently disney  and marvel studios did say that they are  taking the necessary precautions during  this pandemic  and the reshuffling of the schedule of  marvel's phase 4 to make sure that the  mcu keeps its continuity and everything  flows  and to make sure that there are no  spoilers with anything that comes out  originally black widow was supposed to  be the first film released followed by  the falcon and the winter soldier the  eternals shang chi  and then one division but as of right  now one division is going to be the  first mcu phase 4 project released in  january of 2021  most likely followed by the falcon and  the winter soldier and then black widow  so the order is off but marvel studios  assures us that they're going to make  sure there are no spoilers  but as i mentioned marvel studios  executive vice president victoria alonso  was recently asked in an interview about  whether or not black widow is going to  go to disney plus premier access or not  and she ended it on a very interesting  note but this is what she had to say in  the interview  it seems to me that our films are films  for theatrical distribution  we always said that we believe in  different formats and it's very  important to maintain the custom  the tradition of watching certain films  and community  with avengers in-game we did as usual  every friday before a movie comes out we  go to see it with people who had never  seen it  if you see it with those 500 people or  the thousand people or the 100 people  who were in the cinema  what you feel when you see that movie  with other people is something very  different from what one can feel in the  living room with the four  five or six people who live in your  house so whenever possible and that is  something that health measures  allow us we want our films to be seen in  the cinema  now i think most would agree that if we  had our preference yes we would see  black widows in theaters  granted health measures allow us to as  victoria alonso mentioned the experience  is definitely way different and usually  much better in the theater  however it doesn't really seem like we  have that option and it doesn't really  seem like we're going to have it anytime  soon  states are having shutdowns again and it  seems like many more are about to join  them as well  and that's where that last line of this  interview comes in where she said  so whenever possible and that is  something that health measures allow us  we want our films to be seen in the  cinema well right now  it doesn't seem like health measures are  making it possible  it really doesn't seem possible right  now that black widow can be released in  theaters and actually perform well  and in fact there's a lot of talk right  now about wonder woman 1984 being  released on hbo max  and that is because warner brothers  feels like it may perform better on hbo  max than in the theaters due to all the  recent states that have had to shut down  again  and as bob chapeck said mulan performed  very well  even despite the controversy and he said  that they're going to talk about it more  on december 10th during investors day  where we 